      speech: "Here Workspace gets a domain configuration for equipment maintenance. The panels connect work orders, assets, locations, crews and the available safe actions. What matters to me here is the shared context. The agent doesn't work with an abstract text description of the task, separate from the interface. It reads the same current context that is in front of the person. Actions also must not be arbitrary. The interface declares what can be done with a specific object and which restrictions apply right now. Because of this, the working environment can not only show information but also accompany the process itself. It can explain the sequence of actions, highlight a risk or require confirmation before a critical step. So for me this demo is not only an example of an interface for Maximo. It tests the Workspace architecture on a complex corporate process. The XR version tests the same principle without being limited to a flat screen. The task context, the interface and the related physical object can be placed in one space. Real Maximo data, authorization and APIs are connected through a separate integration layer. The Workbench itself remains a demonstration project and an alpha version of the architecture.",
